Render validated Cue JSON from its structured model in its matching native subtitle format.

Usage:
  cueson [global options] render [options] INPUT.cueson.json --to FORMAT

Options:
  --to FORMAT        Select srt or vtt.
  -o, --output PATH  Write native output to PATH instead of stdout.
  -f, --force        Replace an existing regular output file.
  --strict           Reject known non-representable model content.

Global options:
  -q, --quiet  Suppress informational and success diagnostics.
  --silent     Suppress every non-error diagnostic.
  --no-color   Disable diagnostic color.
  -h, --help   Show help.
  --           End option processing; following paths and operands remain literal.

Notes:
  Format aliases: subrip for srt; webvtt for vtt.
  --output - selects stdout. --force requires a filesystem output.

Streams:
  stdout  Canonical native bytes unless a filesystem output is selected.
  stderr  Ordered warnings and errors allowed by the global diagnostic filters.

Exit codes:
  0  Command or explicit help completed successfully; warnings may be present.
  1  An accepted operation failed during processing, cancellation, or runtime I/O.
  2  Command syntax, an operand, an option, or a pre-execution requirement was invalid.

Examples:
  cueson render captions.srt.cueson.json --to srt
  cueson render captions.vtt.cueson.json --to vtt --output captions.vtt
